{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nMaking OperationSnapshot authoritative for LLM operations (gaudy-working-mantaray) migrates `LLMConfig.from_env` call sites and threads a snapshot-derived projection through the gate/workflow entry points. `src/rebar/llm/config.py` (799 LOC) and `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py` (796 LOC) are within a few lines of the hard 800-LOC module-size cap (`.github/module-size-limit.txt`), so that threading would breach the CI module-size gate on first edit.\n\nCreate headroom FIRST via behavior-preserving extraction along existing call-graph seams. This story adds no snapshot-threading logic; it only relocates existing clusters.\n\n## Approach\n\n- `llm/config.py`: move `_env_truthy`, `_read_llm_file_table`, `_llm_str_source`, `_llm_str`, `_llm_int`, `_llm_float`, `_llm_drain_mode` into a new sibling `llm/config_readers.py`. `config.py` re-imports all of them (`from .config_readers import (...)  # noqa: F401`) at module top, mirroring the existing `gate_context` re-export pattern (config.py L41-47). `LLMConfig.from_env` (the sole caller) is NOT moved, so its bare-name lookups resolve through `config.py`'s own namespace — this is what keeps the ~15 existing `monkeypatch.setattr(rebar.llm.config, \"_read_llm_file_table\", ...)` seams live. `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py`'s direct `_read_llm_file_table` import keeps working via the re-export.\n- `llm/plan_review/__init__.py`: move ONLY the five pure leaves — `_apply_floor_to_verdict`, `_score_floor_novelty`, `_apply_completion_floor_to_verdict`, `_classify_completion`, `_group_blocking_fix_units` — into a new sibling `llm/plan_review/floors.py`, re-imported (`from .floors import (...)  # noqa: F401`). `_maybe_apply_rising_floor` and `_maybe_apply_completion_floor` STAY in `__init__.py`: they are the entry points `_run_plan_review` calls, and their internal bare-name calls into the five moved leaves must keep resolving through `__init__.py`'s namespace so `monkeypatch.setattr(plan_review, \"_score_floor_novelty\"/\"_classify_completion\", ...)` (test_plan_review_rising_floor.py, test_completion_floor.py) keeps intercepting. `monkeypatch.setattr(plan_review, \"_maybe_apply_rising_floor\"/\"_maybe_apply_completion_floor\"/\"_group_blocking_fix_units\", ...)` (test_plan_review_sidecar_heldout.py) is unaffected either way since its caller `_run_plan_review` also stays put.\n- **`_verifier_cfg`** stays in `__init__.py` (used elsewhere there too). The two moved leaves that call it (`_score_floor_novelty`, `_classify_completion`) reach it via a **lazy in-function import** (`from rebar.llm.plan_review import _verifier_cfg`), not a module-top-level import — `__init__.py` already does `from .floors import (...)` at its own top, so a reverse top-level import in `floors.py` would cycle. By call time the package is fully initialized, so the lazy import is safe; this mirrors the lazy-import style these two functions already use for `rebar.llm.runner`/`review_kernel.verify`/`passes`.\n\n`LLMConfig`, `review_plan`, and public plan_review imports keep working unchanged.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/` — new sibling modules (`config_readers.py`, `plan_review/floors.py`); import updates only. Does NOT touch `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` (owned by hurt-antigorite-genet).\n- `tests/unit/`, `tests/unit/workflow/`, `tests/external/` — import-path updates only, EXCEPT two consumers that pin a physical path/text and must be repointed:\n  - `tests/unit/test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py` AST-parses `config.py`'s source TEXT by path (`_CONFIG_PY`) to enumerate `_llm_*` helpers; repoint `_CONFIG_PY` to `config_readers.py` (or also parse it) so the moved names keep being found.\n  - `tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py`'s `_EXPECTED_RUN_REQUEST_SITES` hard-codes `'llm/plan_review/__init__.py::_score_floor_novelty'`; update to `'llm/plan_review/floors.py::_score_floor_novelty'`.\n\n## Testing\n\nExisting llm/plan-review suites (`tests/unit/`, `tests/unit/workflow/`, `tests/external/`) pass unchanged — every `monkeypatch.setattr(rebar.llm.config, \"_read_llm_file_table\", ...)` site and every `monkeypatch.setattr(plan_review, \"<floor-helper>\", ...)` site (rising-floor, completion-floor, completion-floor-e2e, blocking-fix-unit-grouping, sidecar-heldout tests) keeps intercepting the same call. The two path-pinning consumers above are updated and continue to pass. Module-size gate, complexity ratchet, lint, typecheck pass. No new CI-provider/network/Docker dependency.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `config.py` and `plan_review/__init__.py` are each <= 700 LOC via extraction into `config_readers.py` / `plan_review/floors.py` only.\n- [ ] No new module < 100 LOC; no mechanical split.\n- [ ] Every existing monkeypatch seam on a moved helper via its ORIGINAL module keeps intercepting the same call site.\n- [ ] `test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py`'s `_CONFIG_PY` control and `test_subcall_class_selection.py`'s `_EXPECTED_RUN_REQUEST_SITES` entry are updated to the new locations and pass.\n- [ ] `floors.py` reaches `_verifier_cfg` via a lazy in-function import; no top-level circular import with `__init__.py`.\n- [ ] Behavior unchanged across `tests/unit/`, `tests/unit/workflow/`, `tests/external/`.\n- [ ] `model_classes.py`'s `_read_llm_file_table` import keeps working unchanged.\n- [ ] `llm/runner.py` untouched.\n- [ ] Module-size gate, complexity ratchet, lint, typecheck all pass."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788037874489631663,"uuid":"26d42b75-54ff-4bb7-b6e6-a6e4132e1ff7"}